{
  "case_id": "2001-01-651",
  "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JPMorgan Chase Bank",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioner, JPMorgan Chase Bank, submits it clearly does. It is well-settled that the term, citizens and subjects, applies to corporations and not just natural persons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is this a question of Federal law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JPMorgan Chase Bank",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United Kingdom reserves the right to review, approve, and ultimately disapprove any statute that is enacted in the British Virgin Islands, which is a right that they do exercise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The United States submits that corporations organized under the United Kingdom overseas territories are citizens or subjects of a foreign State for purposes of alienage diversity jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: You're now relying on English law, I take it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United Kingdom",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ALBERT: Well, actually, the British Nationality Act carves out classes of citizens, and classes of subjects, and persons who are neither citizens nor subjects, so in fact it --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Does it make them subject -- subjects?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United Kingdom",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ALBERT: They belong to the United Kingdom, but that does not answer the statutory question at issue here, because even if they belong to a kingdom, even if they belong to the United Kingdom, that does not make the citizens or subjects of the kingdom."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: How does that affect a corporation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. ALBERT",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that a -- that applying -- that the proper way to apply the Letson principle here is that a British Virgin Islands Corporation should never be subject to diversity jurisdiction precisely because the presumption is that its shareholders have opted for British Virgin Islands status rather than opted for British status."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: That's what I'm putting to you, because the statute uses the same term, citizens or subjects."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What about Canadians? Until Canada domesticated its constitution, I suppose for most of the 19th Century Canadians were not subjects of the Crown?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. REID",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF SARAH L. REID ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. REID",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I will try to be brief. I would like to separate the inquiry between corporations and then address natural persons. Corporations are incorporated through the laws of their legislative district."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. REID",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Kingdom's brief details quite clearly how the corporations are incorporated, rather like our States, corporations in Northern Ireland are incorporated under the laws of Northern Ireland. As I understand respondent's argument, that would make them stateless entities, because they are not actually incorporated in Scotland, Wales, or the United Kingdom. Clearly, that is an absurd result, given the presence of the British --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-651",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2e96706a298b193dc8af9123e17beb4bae8df94c42a2cc71ce52dfb83bbd4bb5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2e96706a298b-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: Thank you, Ms. Reid. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
